From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RDK-BPI EasyMesh Investigation <noreply@example.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 22:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi_hal_send_mgmt_frame: use the interface BSSID

wifi_hal_send_mgmt_frame() always puts ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff in address 3,
including for unicast action frames sent by an AP.  cfg80211 rejects that
frame with -EINVAL before it reaches mac80211:

  nl80211: Frame command failed: ret=-22 (Invalid argument) (freq=5180)

The EasyMesh steering request had already selected the correct source VAP,
destination STA, and operating frequency, but an independent monitor capture
contained no action frame.

Use the AP interface MAC as the BSSID for AP-mode transmissions.  For a STA
interface, use its associated backhaul BSSID.  Address 1 remains the caller's
destination and address 2 remains the interface MAC.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 wifi_hal.c | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/wifi_hal.c b/wifi_hal.c
index 0f049f4..1b68868 100644
--- a/wifi_hal.c
+++ b/wifi_hal.c
@@ -4680,12 +4680,10 @@ int wifi_hal_send_mgmt_frame(int apIndex,mac_address_t sta, const unsigned char
     wifi_interface_info_t *interface;
     u8 *buf;
     struct ieee80211_hdr *hdr;
-    mac_address_t bssid_buf;
     int res = 0;
 #ifdef HOSTAPD_2_11 // 2.11
     int link_id = 0;
 #endif
-    memset(bssid_buf, 0xff, sizeof(bssid_buf));
     
     buf = os_zalloc(24 + data_len);
     if (buf == NULL)
@@ -4702,7 +4700,11 @@ int wifi_hal_send_mgmt_frame(int apIndex,mac_address_t sta, const unsigned char
     }
     os_memcpy(hdr->addr1, sta, ETH_ALEN);
     os_memcpy(hdr->addr2, interface->mac, ETH_ALEN);
-    os_memcpy(hdr->addr3, bssid_buf, ETH_ALEN);
+    if (interface->vap_info.vap_mode == wifi_vap_mode_ap) {
+        os_memcpy(hdr->addr3, interface->mac, ETH_ALEN);
+    } else {
+        os_memcpy(hdr->addr3, interface->u.sta.backhaul.bssid, ETH_ALEN);
+    }
 
     
 #ifdef HOSTAPD_2_11 // 2.11
-- 
2.43.0
